## Lore

The Men-Rall are an ancient and nearly extinct people who sense and shape the
world through electromagnetism. They have no voices, speaking only through
translators that turn their electrical impulses into words, and their fields
let them read, dismantle and mend any machine, however alien, down to the
molecules. They call this mecha-kinesis, and they can also lash out with
bolts of electricity.

They say little of where they came from. Their homeworld is believed to have
been ruined by war or disaster, after which the survivors scattered across the
Megaverse as hired mechanics and technicians. Oddly, they use the machines of
other races but never invent new ones, and some link them to the vanished
Machinists of the Three Galaxies.

Thousands were enslaved by the brodkil and forced to repair their weapons
until the Legion broke the brodkil campaign. In return, Men-Rall technicians
disabled the traps and safeguards the Dakir had built into their soldiers,
clearing the way for the Legion''s mutiny. About a thousand stayed on. They
dislike fighting and avoid it when they can, but they keep the Dakir factories
and medical systems running at Fort Desperado as engineers, doctors and
researchers, and since a soldier jokingly gave one a lab coat as a robe of
honour, they have worn such coats with pride.

## GM Notes

A few hundred Men-Rall also live and work in New Babylon, where their skills
are admired.
', 'published', 'data-script'
